mmandery</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">89</span><span class="rf-text">The Han general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dou-xian">Dou Xian</a> crushes the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-xiongnu">Northern Xiongnu</a> at the Battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/altai-mountains">Altai Mountains</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">188</span><span class="rf-text">Rebels among the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chanyu">chanyu</a>'s followers kill him after he sends his people to fight the Wuhuan for the Han</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">195</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chanyu">chanyu</a> Yufuluo dies at Pingyang and is succeeded by his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huchuquan">Huchuquan</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">216</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-cao">Cao Cao</a> detains <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huchuquan">Huchuquan</a> in the city of Ye and sends his uncle Qubei to manage the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanxi">Shanxi</a></span></li></ol>
